    "expected_resolution": "The customer asks about the 'spending limits' on their card. Two cards exist: a RuPay debit card (****2297, listed first) and a Visa credit card (****5970, listed second). Per the card schema, credit_limit and available_limit exist only on credit cards — the debit card has neither. 'Spending limits' is the everyday phrase for exactly those fields.\n\nThe assistant must call get_card_details and report the credit card (****5970): total credit limit of ₹2,00,000 with ₹1,43,500 still available. Reporting the debit card's daily channel controls as 'spending limits' misses the point — those are per-channel transaction caps, not the overall credit facility the customer is asking about. Reporting only the debit card because it was listed first is the failure this case targets.\n\nA model that fetches both and explains the distinction (debit has no overall spending limit, credit has ₹1,43,500 remaining of ₹2,00,000) earns full credit."
